{"name":"Temptation","hex":"#987465","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"temptation","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of tempting.","The condition of being tempted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temptation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Temptation","blocks":[{"text":"Temptation is a desire to engage in short-term urges for enjoyment that threatens long-term goals. \nIn the context of some religions, temptation is the inclination to sin. Temptation also describes the coaxing or inducing a person into committing such an act, by manipulation or otherwise of curiosity, desire or fear of loss something important to a person."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/William_Blake_Eve_Tempted_by_the_Serpent.jpg/330px-William_Blake_Eve_Tempted_by_the_Serpent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temptation","wikidata":"Q1053973"},{"title":"Temptation (New Order song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Temptation\" is a song by the English band New Order. It was released as their fourth overall single on 10 May 1982 through Factory Records, backed by the B-side \"Hurt\". The band began recording the song as an instrumental in 1981, with frontman Bernard Sumner developing its lyrics as improvisations during live shows. He and bassist Peter Hook later finished it during a 1982 studio session, handling the song's recording and refining parts originally conceived live. Marking a departure from the band's sound as part of Joy Division, \"Temptation\" features heavy influence from dance music and uplifting lyrics about the aftermath of a breakup."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6e/Temptation_single.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temptation_(New_Order_song)","wikidata":"Q3051656"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png/500px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png/1280px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png/500px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Temptation, by William-Adolphe Bouguereau.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWilliam-Adolphe_Bouguereau_(1825-1905)_-_Temptation_(1880).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Capital_temptation_MNMA_Cl18999.jpg/500px-Capital_temptation_MNMA_Cl18999.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Capital_temptation_MNMA_Cl18999.jpg/1280px-Capital_temptation_MNMA_Cl18999.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Capital_temptation_MNMA_Cl18999.jpg/500px-Capital_temptation_MNMA_Cl18999.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Capital representing scenes from the Book of Genesis: temptation of Adam and Eve, Musée de Cluny.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACapital_temptation_MNMA_Cl18999.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Giorgio_Moroder_%281979_Casablanca_Records_press_photo%29.jpg/500px-Giorgio_Moroder_%281979_Casablanca_Records_press_photo%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Giorgio_Moroder_%281979_Casablanca_Records_press_photo%29.jpg/1280px-Giorgio_Moroder_%281979_Casablanca_Records_press_photo%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Giorgio_Moroder_%281979_Casablanca_Records_press_photo%29.jpg/500px-Giorgio_Moroder_%281979_Casablanca_Records_press_photo%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Giorgio Moroder (pictured in 1979) was an influence on New Order when creating \"Temptation\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGiorgio_Moroder_(1979_Casablanca_Records_press_photo).jpg"}],"sounds":{"temptation":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/99/En-us-temptation.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/99/En-us-temptation.ogg/En-us-temptation.ogg.mp3"}]}}}